Johannes Kepler was a unorthodox Lutheran who openly proclaimed Christ presence in the Eucharist who was born in the Holy Roman Empire. 
Kepler was a key figure in the Scientific Revolution, he picked the side of Mathematics over the other side.. the place where math is tested and twisted into... physics. 

He postulated the Kepler conjecture. 
Kepler influenced among others Isaac Newton, providing one of the foundations for his theory of universial gravitation. 
